[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=3.333333mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{red}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{green}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\draw[housegrid,line width=.25pt,xstep=2mm,ystep=3.333333mm] (0,0) grid (6.5,21);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(7,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,22.5);
\foreach \t in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (\t,0)--++(0,-.3);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\t,-.3) {\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text="tick">}$\t$\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}
\foreach \d in {3,6,9,12,15,18,21} {\draw[black] (0,\d)--++(-.15,0);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-.15,\d) {\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text="tick">}$\d$\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text="tick">}$0$\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};
\draw[red,dashed,line width=.5pt] (3.5,0)--(3.5,17)--(0,17);
\draw[green,densely dotted,line width=.6pt] (0,15)--(3.25,15)--(3.25,0);
\draw[blue,line width=.8pt] (0,0)--(1.5,9)--(2.5,9)--(4,21)--(5,21)--(6.5,0);
\fill[red] (3.5,17) circle (2pt);
\fill[green] (3.25,15) circle (2pt);
\path (-1.5,10.5) node[rotate=90] {Distance from start (km)};
\path (3.25,-2.2) node[below] {Time (hours)};
\path (3.25,23) node[above] {Asha's journey};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Follow the red dashed guides: go up from $3.5$ hours to the line, then across to the distance axis. Asha is $17$ km from the start.

(b) Follow the green dotted guides: go across from $15$ km to the rising line, then down to the time axis. She reaches $15$ km after $3.25$ hours.

(c) She stops from $1.5$ to $2.5$ hours and from $4$ to $5$ hours.

Total stopped time:
$\begin{aligned}(2.5-1.5)+(5-4)&=1+1\\&=2\text{ hours}\end{aligned}$

(d) From $5$ to $6.5$ hours the distance from the start falls to $0$, so she returns to the start. This segment is steeper than the first, so she travels faster on the return.

(e) She travels $9$ km out, then $21-9=12$ km farther out, then $21$ km back.

Total distance:
$\begin{aligned}9+12+21&=42\text{ km}\end{aligned}$

Her distance from the start falls on the return, but the total distance she has travelled does not fall.

